    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks, but my issue was not proving the equality directly but rather defining </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">denoteTag</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tag</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TyDenote</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Tag</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toTy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where I believe only a proof that succeeds purely by <code>rfl</code> would enable Lean to prove the definitional equality of types and therefore let me use an element of type <code>Bool</code> where <code>TyDenote (Tag.toTy .b)</code> is expected. Please correct me if I am wrong about this</p>",
